		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=16010&amp;sid=fd9907a37ca4d4b723af5b1ac0135a72#16010"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Fri Nov 01, 2002 3:47 am<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=16010&amp;sid=fd9907a37ca4d4b723af5b1ac0135a72"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Parnhamien turns and smiles at the little Gnome who has offered his greetings and a welcome home. Noting the Concordat badge on diminutive fellow Parnhamien is forced to wonder how many other new faces have joined the ranks of the Angelis that has yet to meet. I have been gone long he thinks, much too long in fact. I have so very much missed the fellowship of this guild and of this place. Why is it I ever left? No matter that is all behind me I am back home now and I shall endeavor to meet as many of new brothers and sisters as I can. &quot;Welladay little cousin&quot;, replies the Half-elf. &quot;Pleased to meet you indeed! But if your referring to myself as 'Great One' then someone has been telling you exaggerated tales of my past indeed. Though flattery will indeed refill your class!&quot; Parnhamien turns his head to Indalis. &quot;Keep my guildmates glass full Indalis whilst he tells me tales of my 'greatness'.&quot; Parnhamien winks at the stout hearted Nabastin. &quot;You were saying...&quot; 
<br />
<i></i><br />_________________<br />Parnhamien Tor'Dainal
<br />
Paladin of Marr
<br />
Elder Concordat Angelis</span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
